 ## Background
-The method originates from research on local-to-global registration for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) and simultaneous color computer-generated holography [S1, S2]. It was introduced to enable camera-in-the-loop optimization by aligning captured wavefronts with SLM patterns [S2]. The mathematical foundation relies on solving homogeneous linear systems via SVD, a standard technique in computer vision for homography estimation [S1].
+The method is applied in local-to-global registration for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) to enable differentiable parameter estimation [S1]. It is also used in simultaneous color computer-generated holography to align captured wavefronts with SLM patterns for camera-in-the-loop optimization [S2]. The mathematical foundation relies on solving homogeneous linear systems via SVD, a standard technique in computer vision for homography estimation [S1].
 
